    "results_or_conclusions": [
        "The SAIL project aims to assess the current state of access to physical activity and the natural environment for older populations in Norfolk.",
        "Policy frameworks from health care, social care, physical activity, and environment sectors contribute towards achieving the project's objectives.",
        "Physical activity guidelines recommend 150 minutes of moderate exercise or 75 minutes of vigorous exercise per week, combined with muscle strength exercises two times a week for those prone to falling.",
        "Falls prevention programs such as Otago and FaME are provided in the Age UK guide. Physical activity has been shown to reduce falls by up to 54% when balanced and progressive.",
        "Public health priorities include utilization of outdoor space, social isolation, health-related quality of life for older people, hip fractures, and emergency hospital admissions due to falls."
    ],
    "possible_value_for_knowledge_platform": "[\"The document provides a comprehensive overview of the SAIL project's objectives and policy frameworks in Norfolk.\", 'It includes detailed physical activity guidelines and fall prevention strategies that can be used as reference for similar projects.', 'The document highlights the importance of addressing gaps in access to physical activity and natural environments for older populations, which can inform future research and interventions.']",
